**Proof.** Retain $B$ occurrences with $b+\eta<d$ and replace their births by $b+\eta$. Zero extension gives an injective natural trim inclusion whose range at $t$ equals the actual image from $t-\eta$ to $t$. The range condition lifts it through $m_t$ by the inverse of the domain-to-range equivalence. Cancelling $m$ proves naturality. The ordered monomorphism injection from this trim to $A$ sends the first $k+1$ occurrences below any long $B$ occurrence into $A$ occurrences with birth at most that occurrence's birth plus $\eta$. This forces the fixed ordinal-$k$ occurrence to exist and satisfy the bound. Short matched occurrences satisfy the bound by positivity and equal death. Essentials remain in the trim; zero trimming retains every positive occurrence.

